---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Calculator from '../components/Calculator.astro';
import {byId} from '../data/routes';
import {calculatorTasks} from '../data/calculator-tasks';
---
<Base home title="Quilt Studio — Better Quilt & Fabric Calculators with Cut Plans" description="Plan a quilt in one place. Calculate backing, straight binding, batting and materials from real cutting diagrams, with printable shopping lists and free local project files.">
<div class="page-shell">
<section class="page-intro page-intro--home" data-ui-hero>
 <div class="page-heading">
  <span class="eyebrow-with-line">— THE MAKER'S TOOLKIT</span>
  <h1>Less guessing.<br/><span class="hero-emphasis">More making.</span></h1>
  <p>Every quilting project begins with a little math. Bring together your fabric, finished dimensions, overage and seam requirements in one thoughtful, free planning workspace.</p>
  <div class="feature-pills"><span>✓ Physical cutting plans</span><span>✓ No account</span><span>✓ Local project files</span></div>
  <div class="hero-actions"><a class="hero-main-cta" href="#calculator-workspace">Start with your quilt <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="hero-sub-cta" href="/calculators/">Explore the full planner</a></div>
  <p class="hero-reassurance">Free tools · No sign-up · Your measurements stay on this device</p>
 </div>
 <div class="mini-feature mini-feature--crafted"><div class="mini-top"><span>MEASURE TWICE, CUT ONCE</span><span>QUILT STUDIO / 2026</span></div><img src="/images/hub.webp" width="640" height="420" alt="Original illustration of patterned fabric squares arranged in a quilting cutting workspace" fetchpriority="high" loading="eager"/>
  <svg class="hero-thread" viewBox="0 0 580 280" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M-12 185 Q 75 95, 154 156 T 321 144 T 598 70" pathLength="100" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="1.2 1.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
  <span class="hero-fabric-seal" aria-hidden="true">MADE<br/>TO<br/>MEASURE</span><div class="mini-bottom"><b>Make room for the joy.</b><span>✳ Made to measure</span></div></div>
</section>
<section class="content-block home-workspace-section" style="margin-top:22px">
 <div class="editorial-head"><span class="eyebrow-with-line">— START RIGHT HERE</span><h2>Your next quilt, in one place.</h2><p>Try the live 60 × 80 inch CENTER-size example with a 3-inch finished border on each edge, producing a 66 × 86 inch outside quilt. The calculator verifies rectangular cutting geometry against entered fabric widths; real-paper scale and physical fabric cuts still require manual checks.</p></div>
 <Calculator tool="hub" sample={byId('hub').sample}/>
</section>
<section class="content-block tool-choice" data-tool-choice>
 <div class="editorial-head"><span class="eyebrow-with-line">— FIND YOUR CALCULATOR</span><h2>What would you like to calculate?</h2><p>Choose by the actual fabric-cutting problem. Every question leads to one calculator, not a duplicate keyword page.</p></div>
 <nav class="task-grid" aria-label="Find a quilt calculator by your cutting task">
 {calculatorTasks.map(task=>{
   const route=byId(task.id);
   return <a class="task-card" href={'/'+route.slug+'/'} data-task={task.id}>
      <span class="task-card-type">{task.label}</span>
      <strong>{task.question}</strong>
      <span class="task-card-detail">{task.detail}</span>
      <span class="task-card-link">Use the {route.nav.toLowerCase()} tool <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span>
    </a>;
 })}
 </nav>
</section>
<section class="sample-block"><div><span class="eyebrow-with-line">— WHY WE MADE THIS</span><h2>Calculations that respect the fabric.</h2><p>A square-inch area estimate can hide impossible cuts. Quilt Studio checks usable width, grain direction and actual rectangular placement before giving you a purchase quantity. Where sewing geometry is unverified, the tool tells you clearly instead of guessing.</p><a href="/calculators/">View all planning tools ↗</a></div><span class="sample-icon" aria-hidden="true">✳</span></section>
</div>
</Base>
